[b][size=5]Quickslot[/size][/b]

Equipment and consumable shortcut groups with a configurable HUD. Tap a group key to equip or use its remembered entry. Hold, browse and release to select another.

[b]Features[/b]
[list]
[*]Up to eight groups for weapons, armor, shields, spells, scrolls, potions, poisons, food, powers, shouts and ammo.
[*]Searchable hand combinations, including smart weapons and shields.
[*]Groups populated automatically from one or more Skyrim Favorites categories.
[*]Hand selection while browsing, with keyboard, mouse and controller bindings.
[*]Smart weapons by physical damage, shields by armor, ammo by damage and potions by strength or best fit.
[*]Hold-to-browse, tap-to-cycle and combined tap-to-cycle/hold-to-browse group modes.
[*]A dedicated consumable binding for using the last selected potion, food or poison.
[*]Keyboard, XInput, PS4 and experimental VR controls with configurable modifiers.
[*]Independent equipment display with quantity badges, poison indicators, bow ammunition counts, shout timers and power dimming.
[*]Separate keyboard/mouse and controller options for using Quickslot while QuickLoot is open.
[*]Rows, columns, grids, crosses, diamonds, circles, lists and a wheel selector with tile or segmented-ring styles.
[*]Separate scale, text size, opacity and anchored placement for the widget, selector and equipment display.
[*]Themes, icon sets, custom colors, per-group colors and an equipped-item highlight.
[*]A preset manager with built-in layouts, automatic presets for controller and keyboard, Undo, automatic saving and menu translations.
[/list]

[b]Requirements[/b]
[list]
[*][url=https://skse.silverlock.org/]SKSE[/url] and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/32444]Address Library[/url] matching your game executable.
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/12604]SkyUI[/url] and Microsoft Visual C++ Redistributable, x64.
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/85702]Inventory Interface Information Injector (I4) 1.1.0+[/url] for your Skyrim version.
[*]VR: SKSEVR, [url=https://github.com/alandtse/skyrim_vr_address_library]VR Address Library[/url], [url=https://github.com/Odie/skyui-vr]SkyUI VR[/url] and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/183466]ImGui VR Helper 1.9.4+[/url].
[/list]

Optional integrations: [url=https://github.com/rijosan87/PNGII]PNG Icon Injector[/url] with icon API v1, [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/120352]SKSE Menu Framework[/url], ImGui Icons and Skyrim Souls RE.

[b]Controls[/b]

Open the editor with [b]Shift + \[/b]. Add items in Groups; New creates combinations and smart shortcuts. Changes save automatically.

Hold a group key and use the wheel or Left/Right to browse. Release to select. Ctrl + Left/Right reorders; both actions wrap. Ctrl + a group key adds the right hand; Ctrl + Shift adds the left. Shift + a group key unequips; Alt + a group key removes its shortcut. While browsing, Backspace unequips and Delete removes the highlighted shortcut.

On controller, groups use D-pad directions by default. Hold a group button and browse with the right stick or LB/RB. Release to select, B/Circle to cancel, X/Square to unequip. Hold D-pad Up and press Start/Options to open the editor. The editor supports D-pad focus, right-stick pointer, click/drag and on-screen text entry.

Configure bindings under Controls. Keyboard actions use None or Clear to disable a binding. For Alt-to-walk setups, assign Remove group shortcut to another modifier or None and enable Allow group selection with unused modifiers.

While browsing, choose Equip in right/left hand to equip the highlighted weapon or spell for the current use. Mouse-button and bumper presets are available in the binding settings.

Tap-to-cycle recalls the selected item when returning to a group and advances on further taps. [b]Tap to cycle / hold to browse[/b] cycles on a short release and opens the selector when held. [b]Keep the other hand equipped while cycling[/b], under Controls → General, starts enabled and skips weapon copies held in the opposite hand.

Consumable groups start with tap-to-use and hold-to-choose. Set [b]Consumables → Use selected consumable action[/b] to cycle or browse consumables, then use a separate binding to consume one dose. Bind [b]Use selected consumable[/b] under Controls → Keyboard or Controller. The action starts unbound and uses the last explicitly selected consumable across groups; the equipment display shows that selection.

In Groups, open the Manual dropdown and check the Favorites categories to include. For example, combine Favorite weapons with Favorite shields / torches. The group displays matching favorites once each, in alphabetical order.

[b]Appearance[/b]

Themes include Skyrim silver, Dear Diary Dark, Edge, Minimal, Norden, Nordic, Oathvein, Untarnished and Vel'dun. Appearance has a page each for Theme, Widget, Selector, Equipment and General. Every slider has step buttons and a reset; Reset page and Reset all appearance restore the defaults.

Each display holds on to one of nine screen anchors with a pixel offset. In Position mode, drag or resize a display, nudge it with the arrow keys or LB + D-pad, or center it. Screen area keeps the HUD inside a 16:9, 2:1 or 21:9 area on ultrawide screens.

Presets lists built-in Default, Cross, Diamond and Circle layouts above your own. Rename, duplicate, update and delete presets, preview them, and apply their look, controls or groups. Input device presets switch the look when you change between controller and keyboard.

[b]Equipped highlight[/b] under Appearance → Theme outlines or tints the tile of an equipped item. [b]Wheel style → Segments[/b] under Appearance → Selector turns the wheel into a ring of wedges with the pointed item's name in the center.

Item icons use your installed I4 packs. Original displays their colors; Theme and White apply the selected tint. Smart shortcuts show the item currently selected, combinations show both items, and hand actions use a gauntlet.

Enable [b]Use PNGII icons[/b] under Appearance → Theme to display matching artwork from PNG Icon Injector. I4 supplies the remaining icons.

Enable Show equipped ammunition under Appearance → Equipment to display equipped arrows or bolts and their current count.

The equipment display shows the right hand first, then left hand, consumable and power/shout. Quantities and shout timers appear on icons. Groups and equipment have independent visibility settings.

[b]Downloads and support[/b]

[url=https://github.com/opteron-x86/quickslot-hotkeys]Source and documentation[/url] · [url=https://github.com/opteron-x86/quickslot-hotkeys/releases]Releases[/url]

The DLL targets SE 1.5.97, AE 1.6.x, 1.7.99/1.7.104 and VR 1.4.15. VR support is experimental.

For bug reports, include Quickslot.log, the game version and reproduction steps. Include a crash log for crashes.

[b]Credits[/b]

Item artwork comes from your installed I4 and PNGII packs. Frame/font attribution and dependency notices are in the [url=https://github.com/opteron-x86/quickslot-hotkeys/tree/master/licenses]licenses folder on GitHub[/url].
